    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0702" n="636" xml:id="pg636"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2344<hi rendition="#superscript"
                    >18/25</hi></note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Document Handed by the Japanese Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nomura</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State on September 23, 1941</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1941-09-23">September 23, 1941</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">“equitable basis” means economic activities of a
                    non-discriminatory character which are not monopolistic, exclusive and
                    exploitative, qualified, however, by the inevitable natural limitations referred
                    to in (<hi rendition="#italic">e</hi>) of the reply to questions put by Mr.
                    Hamilton under instructions of Mr. Hull on September 10. Accordingly it goes
                    without saying Japan is not the sole judge in determining what constitutes
                    “Equitable Basis.”</p>
            </div>
        </body>
